      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cresaptown%2C_Maryland"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cresaptown sits on a Pleistocene terrace of the North Branch Potomac River, where a multi‑component prehistoric site (18AG119) was excavated.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://apps.jefpat.maryland.gov/archeobotany/Sites/18AG119.aspx"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The prehistoric site was bisected by railroad tracks; the eastern part was destroyed by a sewage plant and the western part bulldozed for a ballpark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://apps.jefpat.maryland.gov/archeobotany/Sites/18AG119.aspx"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Before 1728, a Shawnee village occupied the area, with families tending maize while warriors hunted and fished.",
